feat 1.0

# SPEC-ADPHND-002 — the handler adapter carries the runner's namespace. SPEC-RT-006 (agreed, ruling
# 58a4ac88) delivers one namespace per spec file to every adapter as a top-level key of the config
# createAdapter receives ({ ...config, namespace }), says the in-process handler's context carries
# `ctx.namespace`, and says the handler adapter "reports the value its context handed out and none
# when the handler never read it" through the optional reportedNamespace(), after which the
# harness refuses the file with NAMESPACE_NOT_HONOURED when the report is not the delivered value.
# SPEC-RT-006 left the handler side unbuilt because it lies outside that spec's touches; this spec
# is that side. The founder ruled "New spec ADPHND-002" (2026-11-09). DRAFT: status draft until the
# founder flips it; nothing is built.
#
# Why the report is a read, not a delivery: a handler that ignores ctx.namespace writes where it
# likes, outside the namespace, and an absence proof (`records []`) would pass while the system does
# the wrong thing (RT-006's worst failure). Reporting what the handler actually read is the only
# signal the adapter has that the handler honoured it.
#
# Driven through adapters/handler/fixtures/probe.mjs (part of the build, inside touches), command
# `ProbeHandlerNamespace { script?, namespace?, harness?, spec? }`:
#  - Script mode (script given): create the adapter as the harness would, with
#    { ...config, namespace } when `namespace` is given and without the key when it is not (an
#    adapter used outside a runner), then run a space-separated script: `invoke:Namespace` (a
#    three-argument handler that returns ctx.namespace), `invoke:Quiet` (a three-argument handler
#    that never touches ctx.namespace), `invoke:Legacy` (the two-argument handler of SPEC-ADPHND-001),
#    `clock:<iso>` (as in SPEC-ADPHND-001), `report` (calls reportedNamespace()). The trace shows each
#    step; `invoke:Namespace` adds ns=<value|none>; `report` adds report=<value|none>.
#  - Harness mode (harness: Namespace | Quiet | Legacy, with spec): build a REAL harness (createHarness
#    with specPath = spec) over fixtures/namespace.config.json, whose response is this adapter with
#    that one command as `Ping`, and run one case. The answer is the trace `case:<harness> passed`,
#    or the harness's refusal as the ERR below.
#
# DECISIONS this draft cannot settle (see the report that accompanies it):
#  D1. TIMING. The harness checks reportedNamespace() right after the response adapter's setup(),
#      before any case, when no handler can have read ctx.namespace; with "none when the handler never
#      read it" every real handler adapter would then be refused on creation. The harness scenarios
#      below therefore assume the check moves: for a response adapter it runs after the case's
#      invoke() returns, as the first thing the case checks, so a refusal precedes the prediction
#      comparison and the case fails with NAMESPACE_NOT_HONOURED. That is an amendment of SPEC-RT-006
#      (harness.ts, not this spec's touches). If the founder prefers the other reading, the adapter
#      reports the namespace its context carries (delivery), the "never read" scenarios and the
#      harness refusal scenarios go, and this spec shrinks to its first four scenarios.
#  D2. A handler run with no namespace in the config (outside a runner): ctx.namespace is absent and
#      reportedNamespace() answers none, which the harness never checks (it only checks when it
#      delivered one). Scenario "outside a runner" pins that.

spec SPEC-ADPHND-002 "Handler adapter: the runner's namespace"
context Toolchain
aggregate Adapters
type infrastructure
status draft

construct:
  handler at adapters/handler/src/index.ts
  touches adapters/handler/**
  needs SPEC-RT-006
  needs SPEC-ADPHND-001
  createAdapter keeps config.namespace. invoke(command, input, actor) calls the handler as
  handler(input, actorContext, ctx) where ctx = { clock, namespace } and namespace is a getter:
  reading it records that the handler read it and answers config.namespace (undefined when the
  config carries none). reportedNamespace() answers the value read by a handler since the adapter
  was created or last torn down, and undefined when none was read (or the config carried none).
  teardown() forgets what was read. Everything else in ctx and invoke is unchanged.

enforce:
  the handler context carries namespace as the value the config delivered
  reportedNamespace answers the value a handler read and none when no handler read it
  a two-argument handler never reads the namespace and so reports none
  rejects NAMESPACE_NOT_HONOURED when a real harness runs a handler that never read the namespace it was delivered

contract:
  input ProbeInput
  response ProbeResult
  error NamespaceError

scenario "the handler context carries the delivered namespace":
  when: ProbeHandlerNamespace { script: "invoke:Namespace", namespace: "s0599e33863c1" }
  predict success:
    response OK ProbeResult { trace: "invoke:Namespace ns=s0599e33863c1" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "the namespace is the same on every invocation and beside a frozen clock":
  when: ProbeHandlerNamespace { script: "invoke:Namespace clock:2026-07-16T00:00:00Z invoke:Namespace", namespace: "s0599e33863c1" }
  predict success:
    response OK ProbeResult { trace: "invoke:Namespace ns=s0599e33863c1 clock:2026-07-16T00:00:00Z invoke:Namespace ns=s0599e33863c1" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "outside a runner the context has no namespace and nothing is reported":
  when: ProbeHandlerNamespace { script: "invoke:Namespace report" }
  predict success:
    response OK ProbeResult { trace: "invoke:Namespace ns=none report=none" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "the adapter reports the namespace a handler read":
  when: ProbeHandlerNamespace { script: "invoke:Namespace report", namespace: "s0599e33863c1" }
  predict success:
    response OK ProbeResult { trace: "invoke:Namespace ns=s0599e33863c1 report=s0599e33863c1" }
    filesystem has []

scenario outline "the adapter reports none when no handler read the namespace":
  when: ProbeHandlerNamespace { script: <script>, namespace: "s0599e33863c1" }
  predict success:
    response OK ProbeResult { trace: <trace> }
    filesystem has []
  examples:
    | script                | trace                       |
    | "report"              | "report=none"               |
    | "invoke:Quiet report" | "invoke:Quiet report=none"  |
    | "invoke:Legacy report" | "invoke:Legacy role=operator report=none" |

scenario "a harness runs a handler that reads the namespace":
  when: ProbeHandlerNamespace { harness: "Namespace", spec: "adapters/handler/namespace.feat" }
  predict success:
    response OK ProbeResult { trace: "case:Namespace passed" }
    filesystem has []

scenario outline "a harness refuses a handler that never read the namespace it was delivered":
  when: ProbeHandlerNamespace { harness: <handler>, spec: "adapters/handler/namespace.feat" }
  predict rejection NAMESPACE_NOT_HONOURED:
    response ERR NamespaceError { code: "NAMESPACE_NOT_HONOURED", detail: matching <detail> }
    filesystem has []
  examples:
    | handler  | detail                                         |
    | "Quiet"  | "no namespace"                                 |
    | "Legacy" | "no namespace"                                 |
